From ac48d3fabc6855bcbe20e283a8f745f43e089cdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:45:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): refuse a tool wider than its slot at the
 command

The slot generator's fit rule (h = width/2 - r - leave, h = 0 allowed)
moves into one pure function, machining2d::slot_centre_band, called by
the generator and by the tool law's door. CreateOperation and
EditOperationLinks (MCP set_tool, the UI's links edit) now refuse a
plain Slot whose tool is too wide, with both sizes and the largest tool
that fits, in the document unit. ChangeTool refuses a diameter edit that
makes a slot's tool too wide. The generator keeps its own refusal.

2D Pocket is left to #3631: its fit needs the generator's region.

Refs #3475

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
